            "review_title": "Review at Bach Duong Coffee",
            "review_text": "Stirlwen\nNoosaville, Australia62 contributions\n1\nA GREAT COFFEE SPOT- AND KID FRIENDLY TOO.\nJul 2018 • Family\nWe were so impressed by Bach Du'o'ng Coffee shop. It is situated only a short walk to the end of Tue Tinh St (opposite the Louisiane Brewhouse) and around the corner. The seating is in leafy area away from the bustle of the main road..and the coffee and service is just great. The staff are young and really helpful.\nOn weekends we also had a choice of a simple breakfast , Bo Kho, scrambled eggs, etc with a bonus coffee or tea for around VND 55,000. ($3.00).\nThe cafe is owned by a school teacher who also holds basic English speaking classes some evenings for locals to enhance their job prospects. \nAnd the bonus for families is the great little play area beneath some steps which has a rice filled \"sandpit\", a short slide. and hundreds of coloured balls to land in. It is always filled with youngsters, Mums, and Dads. \nJust a great place to relax away from the bustle.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten December 16, 2018",
